TinyLFU as it was before upstream libCacheSim commit 759f4ca ("fix bugs in TinyLFU",
2023-08-15). That commit made W-TinyLFU also count an object in its frequency sketch when
it is first inserted into the window.

The authors' published snapshot (cacheMon/NSDI24-SIEVE) contains the fix, but the paper's
Figure 4 TinyLFU points match the code *without* it. We build a second cachesim with this
patch so the paper's TinyLFU can be reproduced. Evidence is in docs/LOG.md (2026-10-01,
verification). No other algorithm is affected.

Apply from external/NSDI24-SIEVE/libCacheSim (done automatically by setup/02_build_simulator.sh):
    patch -p1 < patches/tinylfu-before-759f4ca.patch

--- a/libCacheSim/cache/eviction/WTinyLFU.c
+++ b/libCacheSim/cache/eviction/WTinyLFU.c
@@ -241,8 +241,6 @@ cache_obj_t *WTinyLFU_insert(cache_t *cache, const request_t *req) {
   cache_obj_t *obj = NULL;
   obj = params->LRU->insert(params->LRU, req);

-  minimalIncrementCBF_add(params->CBF, (void *)&req->obj_id, sizeof(obj_id_t));
-
 #if defined(TRACK_DEMOTION)
   obj->create_time = cache->n_req;
 #endif
